what is the multi-annual financial  framework often refer to as MFF it may  sound complicated but it is simply the  --use long term budget it stretches over  several years and funds complex programs  such as Erasmus and Galileo the MFF  determines the amounts that match the  --use priorities this in turn ensures  stability the MFF also sets limits on  how much the European Union will spend  and in which areas the main EU  institutions all work to shape the MFF  EU leaders who meet in the European  Council to provide political guidance  and the Commission the council in the  parliament that complete the process how  does the process work the Commission  makes the initial proposal then it's up  to the council which has a central role  it ensures all EU countries are part of  the agreement next the Parliament is  asked to give its consent once it does  so the council adopts the MFF through a  unanimous vote find out all you need to  know about the MFF and much more on  Concilium 0 / tu  [Music]
 

